From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/intel/fsp2_0: Take the SoC memory settings version
 from Kconfig

FSP_PLATFORM_MEMORY_SETTINGS_VERSIONS mixes a SoC and a mainboard
version into the version of the MRC cache, so that a build whose
coreboot sets the FSP-M UPDs of the memory differently trains again
instead of resuming the training of the build before. Only Apollo Lake
has a fsp_memory_soc_version() of its own: for the other SoCs bits 3:0
are always 0, and raising them takes a code change.

Add FSP_MEMORY_SETTINGS_SOC_VERSION, 0-15, default 0, which the weak
fsp_memory_soc_version() returns, with a prompt on the platforms that
select FSP_PLATFORM_MEMORY_SETTINGS_VERSIONS. A board's defconfig can
then raise it in the build that changes those settings. With the
default the version, and the code, are those of before.

TEST=Configured lenovo/m920x: FSP_MEMORY_SETTINGS_SOC_VERSION=0 in
the .config, so fsp_memory_soc_version() still returns 0 and the
version of the cache is the one of before; the .config of the boards
without FSP 2.0 does not change.
---
 src/drivers/intel/fsp2_0/Kconfig       | 12 ++++++++++++
 src/drivers/intel/fsp2_0/memory_init.c |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/intel/fsp2_0/Kconfig b/src/drivers/intel/fsp2_0/Kconfig
index 0333203eca..8d9a61b37d 100644
--- a/src/drivers/intel/fsp2_0/Kconfig
+++ b/src/drivers/intel/fsp2_0/Kconfig
@@ -269,6 +269,18 @@ config FSP_PLATFORM_MEMORY_SETTINGS_VERSIONS
 	  mainboard versions lets deployed systems invalidate stale training
 	  data when those settings change while keeping the same FSP binary.
 
+config FSP_MEMORY_SETTINGS_SOC_VERSION
+	int "SoC memory settings version (0-15)" if FSP_PLATFORM_MEMORY_SETTINGS_VERSIONS
+	range 0 15
+	default 0
+	help
+	  Bits 3:0 of the memory settings version that is mixed into the
+	  MRC cache version, unless the SoC code provides its own
+	  fsp_memory_soc_version(). Raise it in a build whose coreboot
+	  sets FSP-M UPDs that the memory training depends on differently,
+	  so that the training saved by an older build is done again
+	  instead of being resumed with the new settings.
+
 config FSP_COMPRESS_FSP_S_LZMA
 	bool
 
diff --git a/src/drivers/intel/fsp2_0/memory_init.c b/src/drivers/intel/fsp2_0/memory_init.c
index a7a9bb230d..edaa15303d 100644
--- a/src/drivers/intel/fsp2_0/memory_init.c
+++ b/src/drivers/intel/fsp2_0/memory_init.c
@@ -224,7 +224,7 @@ uint8_t fsp_memory_mainboard_version(void)
 __weak
 uint8_t fsp_memory_soc_version(void)
 {
-	return 0;
+	return CONFIG_FSP_MEMORY_SETTINGS_SOC_VERSION;
 }
 
